From: System Electronics
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] medialib: restore SDR on the active sensor during deinit

IspManager::deinit() builds a default frontend_config_t before restoring SDR.
The default sensor index is SENSOR_0, even when the active profile uses
SENSOR_1. On Astrial H15 this makes shutdown address the disconnected CSI0
path and leaves the ISP configured for the pre-ISP denoise pipeline.

Carry the sensor index from the current profile into the temporary SDR
configuration used for cleanup.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
diff --git a/hailo-media-library/media_library/src/isp/isp_manager.cpp b/hailo-media-library/media_library/src/isp/isp_manager.cpp
--- a/hailo-media-library/media_library/src/isp/isp_manager.cpp
+++ b/hailo-media-library/media_library/src/isp/isp_manager.cpp
@@ -800,6 +800,15 @@ void IspManager::deinit()
 
     frontend_config_t sdr_config{};
     sdr_config.input_config.resolution = m_input_resolution;
+    if (m_config_manager_interactor)
+    {
+        auto current_profile = m_config_manager_interactor->get_current_profile();
+        if (current_profile.has_value() && current_profile.value())
+        {
+            sdr_config.input_config.sensor_index =
+                current_profile.value()->sensor_config.input_video.sensor_id;
+        }
+    }
     bool dual = m_config_manager_interactor && m_config_manager_interactor->is_dual_sensor();
     const auto &desc = dual ? SDR_DUAL_SENSOR_DESCRIPTOR : SDR_DESCRIPTOR;
     switch_mode(desc, sdr_config);
